{
  "id": "21593_gesen",
  "headword": "{下船|げせん}",
  "reading": "げせん",
  "romaji": "gesen",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "disembarkation; getting off a ship",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "disembarkation; getting off a ship; going ashore",
      "explanation": "The act of leaving a ship or boat, either at a port of call or at the final destination. Used in both formal travel contexts and everyday situations involving ferries and boats."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21593_gesen_ex1",
      "japanese": "{乗客|じょうきゃく}は{順番|じゅんばん}に{下船|げせん}した。",
      "english": "The passengers disembarked in order.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21593_gesen_ex2",
      "japanese": "{港|みなと}に{着|つ}いたら{下船|げせん}の{準備|じゅんび}をしてください。",
      "english": "When we arrive at the port, please prepare to disembark.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21593_gesen_ex3",
      "japanese": "クルーズ{船|せん}の{下船|げせん}{手続|てつづ}きに{時間|じかん}がかかったが、{無事|ぶじ}に{上陸|じょうりく}できた。",
      "english": "The disembarkation procedures for the cruise ship took a while, but we managed to get ashore safely.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {下|げ} (down, off) and {船|せん} (ship). The opposite of {乗船|じょうせん} (boarding a ship).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {下船|げせん}する: to disembark\n- {下船|げせん}{手続|てつづ}き: disembarkation procedures\n- {下船|げせん}{許可|きょか}: permission to disembark\n- {下船|げせん}{時間|じかん}: disembarkation time\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {乗船|じょうせん}: boarding a ship — the opposite action\n- {上陸|じょうりく}: landing, going ashore — emphasizes stepping onto land\n- {下車|げしゃ}: getting off a vehicle (train, bus, car)\n- {降機|こうき}: deplaning, disembarking from an aircraft",
